# Refined pipeline

## Catalog (`sources/catalog.toml`)

One `[[document]]` per known file: `id`, `source_id`, `source_url`, `page_url`, `parser`, `status` (`stable` | `review`). Set `school_year` when the file is a single year. Multi-year workbooks (e.g. Act 1 history) omit it.

- `stable` → `refine` downloads (if needed) and parses.
- `review` → download only; do not parse into facts.
- Add the PDE index page to `pa_edu.discover.PAGES` so uncataloged links surface.

## Parsers (`pa_edu/parse_*.py`)

- Take `(path, document_dict)` and return `{table_name: DataFrame}`.
- Put `school_year` and `document_id` from the catalog/`document` record onto every fact row.
- Normalize codes with `pa_edu.codes` (`as_code`, `as_amount`, `as_text`, `read_sheet`, `require_columns`).
- Match volatile headers by stable substrings or patterns when PDE renames columns year to year; still fail if the required column is missing.
- Skip non-rate placeholder rows (e.g. blank mills) rather than storing null facts that look like rates.

## Refine / storage

- Raw cache: `data/raw/<source_id>/<sha256>/`. Same URL + new hash keeps both copies.
- Write every table listed in `refine.COLUMNS` / `SORT`, then apply `sql/model.sql` and `sql/portal.sql`.
- A new `COLUMNS` table needs a one-line `TABLES` blurb in `pa_edu/portal.py` in the same change. A table with no `aun` also goes in `LOOKUP_TABLES` so each county zip still carries it. `tests/test_portal.py` fails if `TABLES` drifts from `COLUMNS`.
- If `pde.duckdb` is locked, parquet may still be good; do not delete the lock or kill the interactive session.

## Grain

Declare an explicit grain (no duplicate keys). Examples: GFB = AUN × year × function × object × program; retax = AUN × year × county × locality. LEA directory comes from EdNA, not from “latest enrollment name.”
